# hunter_v2 — Workflow and Reuse

## Agent execution checklist

When implementing changes:

1. Read the target file and nearby files.
2. Search for existing shared helper/service/use case before creating new logic.
3. Search for similar behavior in sibling apps.
4. Make the smallest safe change.
5. Keep business rules near their current owner, or extract them into a better owner if already too spread out.
6. Add or update focused tests.
7. Run the smallest relevant test target first.
8. Run `uv run ruff check .`.
9. Run `uv run mypy .` when applicable.
10. Avoid unrelated churn.

If time-limited, the minimum acceptable validation is:

- one targeted test command for the touched behavior
- `uv run ruff check .`

## Highest-priority rule: reuse first

Before adding any new filter helper, search helper, service, use case, storage integration, signature integration, permission helper, table/list rendering helper, or text normalization helper — check shared and local modules first.

Default rule:

- extend an existing shared abstraction when safe
- only add a new helper when no existing shared helper fits
- do not duplicate business logic in a second place

## Shared modules to inspect first

### Query params and list filtering

`apps/core/infrastructure/query_filters.py`: `QueryParamFilter`, `apply_query_param_filters(...)`, `apply_is_active_filter(...)`

### Accent-insensitive text search

`apps/core/infrastructure/search.py`: `build_accent_insensitive_lookup(...)`, `build_text_search_query(...)`, `apply_text_search(...)`

### Shared table/list behavior

`apps/core/templatetags/table_tags.py`: `TableColumn`, `TableAction`, `render_table(...)`
`apps/core/presentation/tables.py`: `TableActionDefaults`

### Shared forms, widgets, and normalization

`apps/core/presentation/forms.py`: `CoreForm`, `CoreModelForm`, `TextNormalizationFormMixin`, `AddressFormMixin`, `MultiStepFormMixin`

### Shared presentation mixins

`apps/core/presentation/mixins.py`: `HtmxTemplateResponseMixin`, `HtmxDeleteResponseMixin`, `PageFavoriteMixin`

### Middleware

`apps/core/presentation/middlewares.py`: `RequireFirstWorkshopMiddleware`, `RequestPerformanceLoggingMiddleware`

### Multi-workshop scoping and permissions

`apps/workshops/mixin.py`: `WorkshopScopedMixin`
`apps/workshops/util/workshops.py`: `get_active_workshop_or_404(...)`, `has_workshop_perm(...)`

### Storage and workshop file orchestration

`apps/core/infrastructure/services/storage.py`: `get_storage_service()`, `S3StorageService`
`apps/workshops/services/files.py`: `get_workshop_file_service()`, `save_workshop_logo_atomic(...)`, etc.
`apps/workshops/usecases/upload_file_usecase.py`: `UploadWorkshopFileUseCase`

### Signature and external provider abstractions

`apps/core/domain/contracts/`, `apps/core/infrastructure/providers/`, `apps/core/infrastructure/services/signature.py`

### Core domain value objects and interfaces

`apps/core/domain/value_objects.py`: `Money`, `Percentage`, `Discount`, `CPF`, `CNPJ`, etc.
`apps/core/domain/interfaces.py`: `Repository`, `UnitOfWork`

## Reuse pattern examples

- List views use `apply_query_param_filters(...)` and `apply_text_search(...)` across `customer`, `catalog`, `stock`, `suppliers`, `budget`, `workorder`, and `messaging`.
- Table-driven list views use `TableActionDefaults` across many apps.
- Workshop-scoped views use `WorkshopScopedMixin` across `budget`, `finance`, `workorder`, and `workshops`.
- Workshop file upload/update orchestration has a service + use-case path; do not bypass it.

## Business logic placement

- Views orchestrate request/response.
- Forms validate and normalize input.
- Templates render.
- Services/use cases orchestrate workflows.
- Domain-layer code owns pure business rules when that structure exists.
- Infrastructure code owns Django/ORM/external-provider coupling.

Avoid putting pricing rules in views, duplicating status transition rules, embedding storage rollback logic in views, or putting permission/business decisions in templates.

## Refactoring guide status

`docs/REFACTORING_GUIDE.md` is active direction for new code. It is not yet fully implemented across the whole repository. Respect current runtime structure; avoid large architectural rewrites unless asked.
